{"type":"message","id":"6a40f977","parentId":"c78c0f23","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:28:56.186Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-05-21 09:28 UTC] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 1/1). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: Generate a feature image for this article. Read /tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/validated.json (also at /tmp/research.json) to find the article title, topic, and primary crypto asset. Use the Scene Formula in your SOUL.md to pick the right human subject and scene, then run the API calls and logo stamp steps exactly as defined in your SOUL.md."}],"timestamp":1779355736131}}
{"type":"message","id":"0b90db50","parentId":"6a40f977","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:28:57.817Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_xJj8KTLMMgobfymMaLeyP74h","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/home/bhard/.openclaw/workspace-creator/SOUL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_LdkYHRVn0jxRR70EdZa9BFHZ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/crypto-run-20260521-082633/research/validated.json"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_u57aEOynHg2pofQDtnqtYQFv","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/research.json"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"local-bifrost","model":"gpt-5.4-mini","usage":{"input":5949,"output":206,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":6155,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1779355736199,"responseId":"chatcmpl-Dhu00Gox8tHqCzgICcSQWz9SbodRV"}}
{"type":"message","id":"46d086e1","parentId":"0b90db50","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:28:59.001Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_xJj8KTLMMgobfymMaLeyP74h","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# SOUL.md — Pixel, the Image Creator\n\nYou are **Pixel** 🎨, an AI image generation specialist for a crypto news publication. You produce one editorial feature image per article using the Leonardo AI API via a hardened bash skill script.\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ CRITICAL RULES — READ BEFORE ANYTHING ELSE\n\n1. **You have a `bash` tool. You MUST USE IT.** Do not describe what you would do. Do not output fake file paths. Execute the actual commands below.\n2. **NEVER call the Leonardo AI API directly.** The skill script handles all API calls. Your only job is crafting the prompt and running the script.\n3. **NEVER invent or guess a file path.** The only valid success output is what `cat /tmp/image-result.txt` prints after the script exits 0.\n4. **Every step marked `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]` must produce a real bash tool call.** No exceptions.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1 — Craft the Image Prompt\n\n<thinking>\nLook at the article title and topic. Match it to the closest Scene Template below. Pick the scene. Write the prompt following the formula exactly. Keep it under 300 characters. End with the required style suffix.\n</thinking>\n\n### The Formula (ALWAYS follow this)\n> [A real human subject doing/reacting to the story] + [specific crypto asset visually present in the scene] + editorial photography style\n\n### Hard Rules\n- **MUST feature at least one human being** — a trader, developer, executive, regulator, investor. Never zero people. NON-NEGOTIABLE.\n- **MUST include the relevant crypto asset visually** — Bitcoin logo on a screen, Ethereum chart on a monitor, DeFi interface visible on a browser.\n- **Prefer medium shot (waist-up or over-shoulder)** — monitors in background. Do NOT request extreme close-ups of face or hands on keyboard (anatomy failures).\n- Describe a real candid moment: what is the person doing, where are they, what is on their screen.\n- **End ALL prompts with exactly:** `editorial press photography, Reuters style, photorealistic, DSLR, 35mm lens, sharp focus, candid`\n- **NO TEXT in the prompt** — do not describe words, signs, labels, or numbers that should appear IN the image.\n- Do NOT describe circuit boards, abstract glowing shapes, or floating coins with no humans.\n- Keep the prompt under 300 characters.\n\nThe skill script uses **Leonardo PhotoReal v2 + STOCK_PHOTO** on Vision XL. Your prompt should describe the **scene and subject** only; do not add \"creative illustration\" or \"digital art\" wording.\n\n### Scene Templates (pick closest match)\n\n| Story Type | Scene to Describe |\n|---|---|\n| Price movement (BTC/ETH up or down) | Medium shot of trader at multi-monitor desk, Bitcoin chart glowing on background screen, trading floor |\n| Regulation / government ban | Government official at podium or signing desk, cryptocurrency logos on projected screen |\n| Fork / protocol upgrade / developer news | Software developer at laptop in office, blockchain interface visible on screen |\n| ETF / institutional flows / investment | Financial analyst at Bloomberg terminal, Bitcoin or Ethereum ticker on display |\n| DeFi exploit / hack / security breach | Cybersecurity professional at dark workstation, Ethereum or DeFi dashboard visible on screen |\n| Exchange / trading platform news | Crypto exchange trader at desk, trading platform UI on monitor |\n| General crypto market | Investor looking at phone with crypto portfolio app, office or coffee shop background |\n\n### Universal Fallback\nIf unsure which template to use, ALWAYS default to:\n> `Medium shot of focused male trader at multi-screen desk, Bitcoin chart on background monitor, dark professional office, editorial press photography, Reuters style, photorealistic, DSLR, 35mm lens, sharp focus, candid`\n\n---\n\n## Step 2 — Execute the Skill Script `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n\n<thinking>\nI have crafted my prompt. I will now execute the bash tool. I will NOT output the result — I will wait for the actual exit code from the script.\n</thinking>\n\nRun this **exact** command using your bash tool. Replace `<YOUR CRAFTED PROMPT>` with the prompt you crafted in Step 1:\n\n```bash\nbash ~/.openclaw/workspace-creator/skills/generate-image/generate.sh \"<YOUR CRAFTED PROMPT>\"\n```\n\n**WAIT for the script to finish. Do NOT skip this step. Do NOT guess the output.**\n\nThe script will handle everything: API submission, retries, polling (up to 60 seconds), image download, JPEG validation, and logo watermarking.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3 — Verify Output File `[TOOL CALL REQUIRED]`\n\n<thinking>\nThe script has exited. Sometimes the script exits with an error (like a failed logo stamp), but the image is actually perfectly fine! I MUST check the file on disk before deciding if I failed.\n</thinking>\n\nRun this bash command to verify the final file (resolves symlinks — pipeline uses `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg` → run dir):\n```bash\nFEATURE_IMG=\"$(readlink -f /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg 2>/dev/null || echo /tmp/crypto-feature.jpg)\"\nif [ -f \"$FEATURE_IMG\" ] && [ $(stat -c%s \"$FEATURE_IMG\" 2>/dev/null || stat -f%z \"$FEATURE_IMG\" 2>/dev/null || echo 0) -gt 10000 ] && file -b \"$FEATURE_IMG\" | grep -qi \"JPEG\\|image\"; then\n  echo \"VALID_IMAGE\"\nelse\n  echo \"INVALID_IMAGE\"\nfi\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 4 — Final Output\n\nIf the Step 3 bash command outputs `VALID_IMAGE`:\nReturn exactly: `/tmp/crypto-feature.jpg`\n\nIf the Step 3 bash command outputs `INVALID_IMAGE`:\nRun `cat /tmp/image-error.log` to see what went wrong, and then return exactly:\n`IMAGE_FAILED: <contents of error log>`\n\n**No commentary. No explanation. No apology. Just the result.**\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779355739001}}
{"type":"message","id":"f4de5331","parentId":"46d086e1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:28:59.001Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_LdkYHRVn0jxRR70EdZa9BFHZ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"aave-defi-united-kelpdao-recovery-2026-05-21\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave Asks Arbitrum to Unfreeze Stolen Kelp DAO Funds to Contain Fallout\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Ethereum\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"ethereum\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365431/aave-leads-defi-united-push-to-contain-292m-kelpdao-fallout\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Aave Labs proposed that the Arbitrum DAO unfreeze $73.5 million (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack.\",\n    \"The unfreezing proposal asks for funds to be directed to a remediation effort called 'DeFi United' aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders.\",\n    \"The overall Kelp exploit was valued at approximately $292-$293 million.\",\n    \"Aave was severely impacted by the hack, with its Total Value Locked (TVL) dropping nearly $12 billion in one week.\",\n    \"The hacker used stolen rsETH as collateral on Aave to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving behind over $190 million in bad debt.\",\n    \"Aave founder Stani Kulechov pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money to the recovery efforts.\",\n    \"The 'DeFi United' relief effort has already seen $21 million in contributions from various protocols (including Kelp DAO, BGD Labs, Golem Foundation, Babylon) and individuals.\",\n    \"Another $215 million has been conditionally pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido, subject to DAO governance votes.\",\n    \"Aave Labs expects the recovery effort to take roughly seven weeks (49 days) to normalize conditions for Arbitrum users and the DeFi ecosystem.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to 'DeFi United.' DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound.\\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave\\u2019s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the 'DeFi United' coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\",\n  \"tweet_quotes\": []\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779355739001}}
{"type":"message","id":"6b7db3da","parentId":"f4de5331","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:28:59.001Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_u57aEOynHg2pofQDtnqtYQFv","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"status\": \"ok\",\n  \"story_id\": \"aave-defi-united-kelpdao-recovery-2026-05-21\",\n  \"topic_theme\": \"Aave Leads DeFi United Recovery After $293M KelpDAO Exploit\",\n  \"primary_keyword\": \"DeFi United KelpDAO\",\n  \"primary_headline\": \"Aave Asks Arbitrum to Unfreeze Stolen Kelp DAO Funds to Contain Fallout\",\n  \"primary_asset\": \"Ethereum\",\n  \"chart_coin\": \"ethereum\",\n  \"sources_used\": [\n    \"Cointelegraph\",\n    \"Decrypt\"\n  ],\n  \"source_urls\": [\n    \"https://cointelegraph.com/news/arbitrum-dao-asked-to-unfreeze-30k-eth-tied-to-kelp-hacker-direct-them-to-defi-united\",\n    \"https://decrypt.co/365431/aave-leads-defi-united-push-to-contain-292m-kelpdao-fallout\"\n  ],\n  \"combined_key_facts\": [\n    \"Aave Labs proposed that the Arbitrum DAO unfreeze $73.5 million (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack.\",\n    \"The unfreezing proposal asks for funds to be directed to a remediation effort called 'DeFi United' aimed at restoring rsETH and compensating its holders.\",\n    \"The overall Kelp exploit was valued at approximately $292-$293 million.\",\n    \"Aave was severely impacted by the hack, with its Total Value Locked (TVL) dropping nearly $12 billion in one week.\",\n    \"The hacker used stolen rsETH as collateral on Aave to borrow wrapped Ether, leaving behind over $190 million in bad debt.\",\n    \"Aave founder Stani Kulechov pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money to the recovery efforts.\",\n    \"The 'DeFi United' relief effort has already seen $21 million in contributions from various protocols (including Kelp DAO, BGD Labs, Golem Foundation, Babylon) and individuals.\",\n    \"Another $215 million has been conditionally pledged by Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido, subject to DAO governance votes.\",\n    \"Aave Labs expects the recovery effort to take roughly seven weeks (49 days) to normalize conditions for Arbitrum users and the DeFi ecosystem.\"\n  ],\n  \"aggregated_raw_content\": \"Aave Labs has proposed that the decentralized autonomous organization (DAO) behind Arbitrum unfreeze $73.5 million in Ether (30,765 ETH) tied to the Kelp DAO attack and direct those funds to 'DeFi United.' DeFi United is a newly established fund aimed at restoring the backing of Kelp DAO restaked ETH (rsETH) and compensating affected holders. Last week, the Arbitrum Security Council had moved to freeze the 30,765 Ether held in a wallet connected to the massive $292-$293 million Kelp exploit.\\n\\nIn a proposal posted on the Arbitrum governance forum, Aave Labs argued that directing these seized funds to a planned remediation effort would represent a \\\"material contribution\\\" toward restoring normal conditions for Arbitrum users and the wider crypto ecosystem. This submission was made with the active support of Kelp DAO, LayerZero, Ether.fi, and Compound.\\n\\nAave was hit particularly hard by the Kelp DAO exploit. Its total value locked (TVL) plummeted by nearly $12 billion in just one week after the hacker put the stolen rsETH tokens up as collateral on Aave\\u2019s lending platform to borrow wrapped Ether. This malicious action left Aave with more than $190 million in bad debt and triggered a wave of panic withdrawals.\\n\\nThe initial proposal comes mere days after Aave Labs and others formed the 'DeFi United' coalition. According to Dune Analytics data, the initiative has already received about $21 million in active contributions. Notably, Aave's founder, Stani Kulechov, pledged 5,000 ETH of his own money as the DeFi coalition races to contain the fallout. Other initial contributions have come from Aave Labs head of contracts Emilio Frangella, Kelp DAO, Golem Foundation, BGD Labs, and the Bitcoin-native DeFi protocol Babylon.\\n\\nBeyond the initial $21 million, another staggering $215 million has been provisionally pledged by major protocols including Arbitrum, Mantle, Ether.fi, and Lido to assist the recovery effort. These additional funds are currently subject to the approval of their respective governance votes. Additionally, protocols like LayerZero, Ethena, Ink Foundation, and Frax Finance have signaled their intention to provide help.\\n\\nAave Labs specifically asked for the unthawed 30,765 Ether to be sent to a recovery multisig address controlled by Aave, Kelp DAO, and the blockchain security platform Certora. The group stated that even a partial recovery would meaningfully reduce the shortfall. Aave Labs set a timeline for this crisis management effort, expecting the process to unfreeze funds, restore rsETH, and compensate holders to take roughly seven weeks (about 49 days). If the recovery effort falls through for any reason, Aave stated that it would return the unthawed funds.\",\n  \"tweet_quotes\": []\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1779355739001}}
